# UIKit View Conventions

When creating or editing UIKit views in this project:

- Custom project types written by us must use the `MT` prefix as a namespace, for example `MTPrefixCardView`.
- Do not rename Apple lifecycle/template classes such as `AppDelegate` or `SceneDelegate` just to add `MT`.
- Internal control event handlers must use `XXXClick`, for example `sampleButtonClick`.
- Public callbacks exposed by a view must use closures named `XXXAction`, and the closure parameter must be the view itself.
- If the whole view is tappable, subclass `UIControl` so callers can use `addTarget`.
- For unusual cases, stop and ask before deviating.

Use this structure for custom views:

```swift
// MARK: data property

// MARK: setup

public override init(frame: CGRect) {
    super.init(frame: frame)
    setupSubviews()
    setupViewConstraints()
}

public required init?(coder: NSCoder) {
    fatalError("init(coder:) has not been implemented")
}

private func setupSubviews() {}

private func setupViewConstraints() {}

// MARK: private methods

// MARK: action

// MARK: refresh

public func refreshView(with sampleModel: SampleModel?) {}

// MARK: getter lazy view
```
